    "field": "Arctic amplification",
    "problem": "State-of-the-art climate models struggle to reproduce the observed rate of Arctic warming, systematically underestimating the nearly four-fold amplification since 1979, which indicates the observed warming is either an extremely unlikely event or the models are deficient in representing key Arctic processes.",
    "method": "This paper quantifies the Arctic amplification ratio by calculating and comparing the linear trends of near-surface temperatures from observational datasets and climate model ensembles for the period 1979\u20132021 to assess how well models simulate the observed four-fold warming.",
    "task": "The task is to quantify the observed Arctic warming amplification since 1979 using multiple datasets and evaluate the ability of state-of-the-art climate models to simulate the nearly four-fold faster warming rate.",
